From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:01:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Linux host: the runtime's 128-bit compare-and-swap, and the
 tests of the instructions Remill patch 0010 lifts (#16)

aot_runtime.cpp: __remill_compare_exchange_memory_128 (lock cmpxchg16b, alignment checked first), for
ldxp/stxp of two X registers.

Tests, each instruction assembled with aarch64-linux-gnu-as, lifted alone and compared with Unicorn
(values, NZCV, memory, FPSR): pair exclusives (and four threads adding to both words of a pair), the
saturating narrows with the QC flag, FRECPE and FRECPX with their flags, half precision conversions in
the four rounding modes, register-form CCMN. lift_coverage.py prints which forms Remill lifts, by family.

The tests that used a register-form ccmn as "an instruction Remill cannot lift" (test_aot_stub,
test_aot_cache, test_elf_module, module_fixture) use cls instead, which Remill still does not lift.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: The runtime side of Remill patch 0010 (128-bit compare-and-swap) and the tests that compare the new instructions with Unicorn
Issue: Sunshine-Off/NX2Linux#16

